%description:

Tcp.softIcmpErrorsAbortSetup:rfc -- a Time Exceeded does not abort the setup: the SYN goes again.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "true: a soft ICMP error ... aborts a connection in SYN_SENT or SYN_RCVD, as
Linux (tcp_v4_err(), tcp_v6_err()) and RFC 5461 section 4 describe; false: RFC 9293 MUST-56, a
soft error never aborts a connection".

The classes: rfc (false, the default) and linux (true, the value of LinuxTcp). The code:
TcpConnection::processIcmpv4Error() aborts a connection in SYN_SENT or SYN_RCVD at a hard
error; with true, also at a soft error: a Destination Unreachable with the codes 0, 1 and 5,
a Time Exceeded and a Parameter Problem. This test separates "rfc" from "linux".

Host under test: host1, behind a router; the tap sets the TTL of the first SYN of host1 to 1,
so the router answers with an ICMP Time Exceeded, a soft error. Observation: level 1, host1 sends the SYN again after the timer of the SYN.

%# parameter: Tcp.softIcmpErrorsAbortSetup
%# class: rfc
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.softIcmpErrorsAbortSetup
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpSoftIcmpErrorsAbortSetupRfc")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true").nth(1).set("ipv4.timeToLive", "1")
                     .describe("the first SYN of host1: a TTL of 1, so that the router sends a Time Exceeded"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .describe("the second SYN of host1, after the timer of the SYN")
             .within(1.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpSoftIcmpErrorsAbortSetupRfc compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.softIcmpErrorsAbortSetup = false    # the parameter under test
network = inet.protocoltest.TapRouterNetwork
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpSoftIcmpErrorsAbortSetupRfc: PASS
